# FreeSail: the captain's orders for the passage of gate 5b in thick weather (spec M5
# §20; package 33a). The same book as the clear passage's for the soundings; no bearings
# to be had; the course for Falmouth shaped by account when the run since noon says she
# is off the Lizard (thirty miles: judgement from the noon's account, some forty miles
# south of the Lizard by the reckoning), and the ship hove to at the first land seen,
# which in a mile of fog is close aboard and where the reckoning's errors have put her.

standing order "bring to for soundings": at noon then heave to
standing order "soundings": when the speed is under 3 knots and the distance run since noon is under 5 miles then heave the deep-sea lead
standing order "fill away after the cast": at a sounding, if the distance run since noon is under 5 miles then fill away
standing order "stand on": at filled away then steer N

# The landfall made wrong: by account she is off the Lizard at thirty miles since noon,
# and the course for Falmouth is shaped from the reckoning.
standing order "off the Lizard by account": when the distance run since noon exceeds 30 miles then shape a course for Falmouth

# The lead going every glass once she believes herself closing the land, and at the
# first land seen, close aboard in a mile of fog, she stands off to the southward: a lee
# shore in thick weather is hauled off from, not lain to under (Luce 1866 ch. XXIV; the
# lead, 2026-09-30: hove to a mile off Black Head she forereached on to it in twelve
# minutes). The gate ends with her standing off, the account eleven miles wrong.
standing order "lead going": every glass, if the distance run since noon exceeds 30 miles and the land is not in sight then heave the lead
standing order "the land": when the land is in sight then steer S
